{"strongs": "H2435", "word": "חִיצוֺן", "translit": "chi.tson", "root": "חוץ", "morph": "H:A", "pos": "adjective", "gloss": "outer, external", "definition": "חִיצוֺן adjective outer, external (opposed to פְּנִימִי ) feminine חִיצוֺנָה (for חוֺצוֺן , by dissimilation, Ba NB xxix Phil BAS ii. 2. 362 Ges «GKC:27»§ 27 . 3 R 6) — 1. 2Kgs 16:18 מְבוֺא הִמֶלֶךְ הַחִיצוֺנָה the outer entry of the king (namely to the Temple), Ezek 44:1 the outer gate of the sanctuary, החצר החיצונךְ the outer court (of the Temple) Ezek 10:5 ; Ezek 40:17 ; Ezek 40:20 ; Ezek 40:31 ; Ezek 40:34 ; Ezek 40:37 ; Ezek 42:1 ; Ezek 42:3 ; Ezek 42:7 ; Ezek 42:8 ; Ezek 42:9 ; Ezek 42:14 ; Ezek 44:19 ; Ezek 44:1 ; Ezek 46:9 ; Ezek 46:20 ; Ezek 46:21 , compare Esth 6:4 (of Ahasuerus'palace), 2Chr 33:14 ׳ חוֺמָה ח an outer wall (built by Manasseh for the עִיר דָּוִיד ); הַחִיצוֺן absolute, in לַחִיצוֺן 1Kgs 6:29 ; 1Kgs 6:30 , בַּחִיצוֺן Ezek 41:17 ( הַבַּיִת being understood) of the outer (part of the Temple), i.e. the Holy Place (compare פְּנִימִי , פְּנִימָה , of the Holy of holies). 2. figurative outward, external הַמְּלָאכָה הַחִיצוֺנָה Neh 11:16 ; 1Chr 26:29 , of business not distinctively sacred, in which Levites were engaged (compare The Late Hebrew use of ׳ ח to denote extra-canonical , as Sanh. 1Chr 10:1 [Jost, 1Chr 11:1 Surenh.] ספרים החיצונים ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2631')\">BDB2631</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2435')\">H2435</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2630')\">BDB2630</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2632')\">BDB2632</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>חִיצוֺן</bdbheb> <b>adjective</b> <highlightword>outer, external</highlightword> (opposed to <bdbheb>פְּנִימִי</bdbheb>) feminine <bdbheb>חִיצוֺנָה</bdbheb> (for <bdbheb>חוֺצוֺן</bdbheb>, by dissimilation, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ba')\">Ba<sup>NB xxix</sup></lookup> Phil<sup>BAS ii. 2. 362</sup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ges')\">Ges</lookup><sup>«GKC:27»§ 27</su